|YKBThe Charlatan Illusionist|000

|000Charlatan Illusionists are notorious scam artists; they prefer not
|000to work any harder than absolutely necessary. Using their charm and
|000a little brains, they make their way throughout Darkwind through
|000haggling, trickery, and a dose of alchemy science.
|000
|000The illusionist's abilities are centered around making things look
|000better or worse than they actually are. Because they often find they
|000need to remove themselves from a sticky situation quickly, they also
|000have honed their ability to avoid attacks, and to cover their
|000tracks. Charlatans in this particular focus will find their charisma
|000will play a large role in how effective their skills will be.
|000
|000Use '|GKBchelp commands|000' for a list of commands.
|000
|000Above and beyond the common skills associated with the charlatan, one
|000with a focus in Illusion can greatly increase the effectiveness of
|000some skills as well as the ability to learn some new tricks.
|000
|000An Illusionist may increase his ability in any of these skills:

|CKBEconomics|000                   Charlatans know what to say around
|000                            town to get the best deals, and how
|000                            to get the most for their goods. With
|000                            this, a charlatan can make sure to
|000                            get the most out of every coin.
|000
|CKBCritical Hit|000                Using their training in the workings
|000                            of anatomy, charlatans know just
|000                            where it will REALLY hurt.
|000                            |RKBRequires the 'Appraise' skill|000
|000
|CKBDazzle|WK0                      A simple magic trick that can
|000                            distract an opponent, decreasing their
|000                            ability to fight.
|000
|CKBVentriloquism|000               A charlatan can dish out some nasty
|000                            words. By throwing their voice, the
|000                            charlatan can sometimes trick a
|000                            mark into attacking someone nearby.
|000
|000The Illusionist also can learn these useful skills:
|000
|CKBBlur|000                        Temporarily increase dodging with some
|000                            fancy footwork and magic.
|000                            |RKBRequires the 'Dazzle' skill|000
|000
|CKBBluff|000                       You can make themself appear to be a lot
|000                            bigger of a threat than they actually
|000                            are. Sometimes it might even work.
|000                            |RKBRequires the 'Dazzle' skill|000
|000
|CKBEvade Hunter|000                Cover your tracks to lose someone on
|000                            your tail.
|000
|CKBEscape|000                      Escape in a confusion of sight, sound,
|000                            and smoke.
|000                            |RKBRequires the 'Evade Hunter' skill|000
|000
|CKBSense Watcher|000               A sixth sense can warn you of danger.
|000                            |RKBRequires the 'Escape' skill|000
|000
|CKBConfuse|000                     Distract an opponent so they cannot
|000                            effectively attack.
|000                            |RKBRequires the 'Ventriloquism' skill|000
|000                            |RKBRequires level 20 to use|000
|000
|CKBShadow Illusion|000             With some clever illusion magic, you can
|000                            animate some gold coins to fight for your.
|000                            |RKBRequires the 'Confuse' skill|000
|000
|CKBSucker Punch|000                Sucker Punch (spunch) and really haul
|000                            back and wail on someone when they
|000                            aren't looking. Confused targets are
|000                            typically easier to hit, and a better
|000                            weapon can do more damage.
|000                            |RKBRequires the 'Critical Hit' skill|000
|000
